# Performance Rules

Performance work must preserve correctness.

## Database

- Avoid N+1.
- Paginate.
- Select only required columns.
- Use indexes based on query plans.
- Avoid unbounded joins.
- Cache only data that is safe to cache.

## Redis

Use Redis for:

- caching
- rate limiting
- queue broker
- short-lived coordination

Do not use Redis as the source of truth for financial/accounting state.

## Search

Meilisearch is a read model. Do not write business state only to search.

## Next.js

- Prefer Server Components.
- Avoid unnecessary client hydration.
- Optimize images.
- Stream where appropriate.
- Cache only when invalidation semantics are understood.

## Queues

Move slow non-critical side effects out of request paths:

- email
- notifications
- search indexing
- analytics delivery
- some media processing

Do not move transaction-critical invariant enforcement to asynchronous jobs.
